  "slug": "single-nucleotide-precision-67f0",
  "summary": "Cell-free DNA now reports tissue somatic mutations non-invasively as InDel and chromosome-level analyses refine mutational process attribution.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these preprints is the resolution at which somatic change is measured in tissues, from chromosome number and structure to indel classes. In acral melanoma, single-cell chromosome counts range from 25 to over 200, with continuous numerical and cryptic structural fluctuation linked to MMBIR repair. Two cell-free DNA studies extend detection of clonal mosaicism and liver-derived somatic mutations to chronic liver disease and ulcerative colitis, reporting etiology-linked patterns without tissue sampling. A genome-wide InDel taxonomy of 887 multiple myeloma genomes adds a distinct class of mutational processes, including a TXNDC5 hotspot and an association with treatment outcome. A benchmarking study of sample mispairing detection tools addresses sample-identity verification in multimodal cancer datasets, a methodological concern distinct from mutational processes themselves.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
